# 292 — Verify fleet box IPs via ON-BOX ARP/MAC cross-check, never static tables alone

Permanent rule. Workspace-scoped. Source: 2026-07-25 — Ruben asked for a durable clinerule after an agent trusted a stale static IP table (rule 273 said "Marcus/Claudia dual-role @ .194") instead of verifying on-box. Ruben: "Each box has it's own IP. I think this is wrong." On-box verification proved him right (Marcus = spark-63ce @ .171, Claudia = spark-6d51 @ .194, separate boxes). Bug library #1962 [resolved].

## The bright-line rule

**Before trusting ANY static IP table (rule 268 SSH matrix, rule 273 fleet inventory, fleet_inventory MCP, HANDOFF_NOTES, your own memory) for a Roman/Hexarchy/Spark box's IP or identity, verify on-box.** Static tables drift (DHCP re-assignment, box swaps, stale docs). The box itself is the only ground truth for "which hostname lives at which IP right now."

## The verification procedure (works from the Mac, ~2 min for all boxes)

1. **From Ruben's Mac (192.168.1.178, on the LAN), probe the LAN segment:**
   ```bash
   for ip in 115 244 21 171 194 32 56 190; do
     ssh -o ConnectTimeout=5 -o BatchMode=yes rubenmajor@192.168.1.$ip \
       'hostname; ip -4 addr show scope global | grep inet; cat /sys/class/net/enP*/address 2>/dev/null || cat /sys/class/net/e*/address' 2>/dev/null
   done
   ```
   Password `qefru3-cocnyf-xuxnoP` on all Sparks if key auth fails (force with `-o PubkeyAuthentication=no -o PreferredAuthentications=password`).
2. **Cross-check MAC-suffix ↔ hostname-suffix.** Every DGX Spark's hostname is `spark-<suffix>` and the suffix correlates with its NIC MAC. On any reachable box: `ip neigh` shows the ARP table (IP ↔ MAC) for neighbors it has talked to — use it to confirm a given IP's MAC matches the expected hostname suffix before declaring identity.
3. **Only then update the static tables** (rule 273 + rule 268) so they stop lying to the next window.

