## Why the alternatives fail (do not waste turns on them)

- **UniFi UDM API client-list endpoint:** never successfully located on this network. Do not burn turns hunting for it — go on-box instead.
- **WOPR-executed ssh_command to 192.168.1.x:** WOPR cannot route to the 192.168.1.x LAN directly (WOPR reaches Cato/Cesar only via reverse tunnels on localhost :2203-:2206). Run LAN sweeps from Ruben's Mac via `execute_command`, not via the emsu-operations MCP.
- **DHCP/ping sweeps with no hostname read:** an IP answering ping proves a device exists, not which box it is. Always read `hostname` + MAC on-box.

